II. Distinguishing Free Personal Use from Institutional and Commercial Use

1. "Free Personal Use" means use of the Software by a natural person in a personal capacity for their own learning, research, noncommercial personal analysis, software repair or feature development, without performing duties on behalf of an organization, handling an organization's affairs or providing paid services to clients.
2. "Institutional Use" means use by enterprises, government agencies, public institutions, schools, research institutions, social organizations and other organizations, as well as use by individuals acting on their commission, performing duties on their behalf or handling their affairs, regardless of whether the organization is for profit or charges fees.
3. "Commercial Use" includes using the Software to provide casework, consulting, analysis, risk-control or other services for a fee; incorporating it into commercial products, deliverables or commercial services; and receiving compensation through selling, renting or providing services based on the Software.
4. Whether use is Institutional or Commercial Use is determined by its actual purpose and the parties it serves. It does not change because of a personal account, a privately owned computer, personal payment or installation by an employee on their own initiative.

